<div class="partial PartialQuestionContent partial7 of12">
            <div class="full-answer">
<div class="PartialQuestionContent-body">


<div class="full-answer" data-zen="true">

<h3 class="full-answer-label"><a id="full-answer">Full Answer</a></h3>

<span class="full-answer-content"><p>The most concrete argument against cloning is that it is still a nascent technology that is prone to high rates of failure. It is plausible that cloning and related genetic engineering could lead to objectification of human beings by the potential to change undesired traits or start completely anew. In addition, the "slippery slope" of legalizing and accepting cloning as a society may lead to other radical technologies that compromise identity.</p>

<a class="more" href="/web/20161008014634/https://www.reference.com/world-view/explore/ethics" data-unified="{&quot;imagePresent&quot;:true,&quot;resultType&quot;:&quot;questionContent&quot;,&quot;providerSource&quot;:&quot;questionContent&quot;,&quot;contentId&quot;:&quot;e810fa4718de64d9&quot;,&quot;globalContentId&quot;:&quot;f6dced6c4af38ec2&quot;,&quot;zoneName&quot;:&quot;center&quot;,&quot;moduleName&quot;:&quot;primaryQuestion&quot;,&quot;moduleInZone&quot;:3,&quot;resultInModule&quot;:1}" data-qo="learnMore" data-unified-assettype="primaryTextLink">Learn more about Ethics<span class="arrow"></span></a>

