<meta name="description" content="Scientists are on the cusp of developing new technologies that could radically change how we\xe2\x80\x99re born and how we die. For instance, by tinkering with specific genes, we might be able to eliminate the risk of diabetes or Alzheimer\xe2\x80\x99s disease. Most likely, we could also create smarter and more beautiful babies. But just because we can do it, should we? As you can imagine, this scientific frontier poses all kinds of thorny ethical questions. And for lots of people, it\xe2\x80\x99s just plain wrong for humans to play God."/>
